# drivers/gpu/conf: the GPU.
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_<NAME>=y in a defconfig builds a driver into the kernel; "standard" files are always built.
# tools/hakios-config.py reads this file; docs/drivers-config.md says what each word means and how it reaches XNU.

driver ADRENO
	file    bsd/dev/hakios.adreno.c
	requires GPUSERVICE
	help    the Adreno 642L of the SC7280 woken step by step (adreno=N), kept for HakiosGPU with gpu=1 or adreno_keep=1
	help    (docs/reference/metal.md). Needs the GPU's firmware from the phone (fw-gpu/)

driver GPUSERVICE
	file    iokit/Kernel/hakios.gpu.cpp iokitcpp
	help    HakiosGPU, the IOKit service Mesa, Metal and the window server draw through. It calls a GPU driver's
	help    hakios_gpu_* (ADRENO, or a device's own such as zeus's A730), so it goes with one of them
	default n
